{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_1>\nimport sys\nfrom math import factorial\n\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ndef A(n, k):\n    return factorial(n) // factorial(n - k)\n\ndef solve():\n    n, mod = map(int, input().split())\n    if n == 1:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    z = [1]\n    total = 0\n    \n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        # Create new array for next iteration\n        new_z = [0] * (i * i // 2)\n        \n        # Update new_z based on current z\n        for j in range(len(z)):\n            for k in range(i):\n                if z[j] > 0:\n                    new_z[i - k - 1 + j] += z[j]\n        \n        # Compute suffix sums (d)\n        d = [0] * (len(z) + 1)\n        for w in range(len(z) - 1, -1, -1):\n            d[w] = (d[w + 1] + z[w]) % mod\n        \n        # Compute prefix sums (e) and weighted prefix sums (f)\n        e = [0] * (len(d) + 1)\n        f = [0] * (len(d) + 1)\n        for w in range(len(e) - 1):\n            e[w + 1] = (e[w] + d[w]) % mod\n            f[w + 1] = (f[w] - w * d[w]) % mod\n        \n        # Calculate contribution for current i\n        current_contribution = 0\n        for jj in range(len(z)):\n            L = jj + 2\n            R = min(len(z) - 1, i + jj)\n            ccc = 0\n            if R >= L:\n                ccc = (ccc + (e[R + 1] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + jj) + (f[R + 1] - f[L])) % mod\n            current_contribution = (current_contribution + ccc * z[jj]) % mod\n        \n        total = (total + current_contribution * A(n, n - i)) % mod\n        z = new_z\n    \n    print(total % mod)\n\nsolve()\n</your_rewritten_code_1>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long factorial(long long n) {\n    long long result = 1;\n    for (long long i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n        result *= i;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nlong long A(long long n, long long k) {\n    return factorial(n) / factorial(n - k);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long n, mod;\n    cin >> n >> mod;\n    \n    if (n == 1) {\n        cout << 0 << endl;\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    vector<long long> z = {1};\n    long long total = 0;\n    \n    for (long long i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n        // Create new array for next iteration\n        vector<long long> new_z((i * i) / 2, 0);\n        \n        // Update new_z based on current z\n        for (long long j = 0; j < z.size(); j++) {\n            for (long long k = 0; k < i; k++) {\n                if (z[j] > 0) {\n                    new_z[i - k - 1 + j] = (new_z[i - k - 1 + j] + z[j]) % mod;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Compute suffix sums (d)\n        vector<long long> d(z.size() + 1, 0);\n        for (long long w = z.size() - 1; w >= 0; w--) {\n            d[w] = (d[w + 1] + z[w]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Compute prefix sums (e) and weighted prefix sums (f)\n        vector<long long> e(d.size() + 1, 0);\n        vector<long long> f(d.size() + 1, 0);\n        for (long long w = 0; w < e.size() - 1; w++) {\n            e[w + 1] = (e[w] + d[w]) % mod;\n            f[w + 1] = (f[w] - w * d[w]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Calculate contribution for current i\n        long long current_contribution = 0;\n        for (long long jj = 0; jj < z.size(); jj++) {\n            long long L = jj + 2;\n            long long R = min((long long)(z.size() - 1), i + jj);\n            long long ccc = 0;\n            if (R >= L) {\n                ccc = (ccc + (e[R + 1] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + jj) + (f[R + 1] - f[L])) % mod;\n            }\n            current_contribution = (current_contribution + ccc * z[jj]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        total = (total + current_contribution * A(n, n - i)) % mod;\n        z = new_z;\n    }\n    \n    total %= mod;\n    if (total < 0) total += mod;\n    cout << total << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.75\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00022384998737834394, -5.602820692729438e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.0006945105269551277, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00016556799528189003, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -7.271740287251305e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.266281055402942e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0009126074146479368, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.02481714077293873, -0.029751690104603767, -0.47411203384399414, -1.3470558769768104e-05, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.0020512747578322887, -9.65590606938349e-06, -0.0009939497103914618, -0.636428713798523, -1.0251946150674485e-05, -7.497983460780233e-05, -2.622600959512056e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.34845468401908875, -1.728519782773219e-05, -0.026316005736589432, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -0.0024273712188005447, -9.894321920000948e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.023250222206115723, -1.883488948806189e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -0.000